-- Passage wg8-argument-writing-p04
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('8f8fdcce-3cf8-5a35-9d02-cbb7d2a40f51', 'wg8-argument-writing-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g8-argument-writing'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Refill Stations for Ridgeview$q$, $q$(1) Each week, the trash cans in our cafeteria fill up with empty plastic water bottles. (2) The district should install water bottle refill stations in every hallway of Ridgeview Middle School. (3) First, refill stations would reduce plastic waste. (4) The environmental club counted the bottles thrown away in the cafeteria for one week and found more than 900. (5) Second, refill stations would encourage students to drink more water during the day. (6) Students who stay hydrated tend to concentrate better in class. (7) Plastic was invented more than a hundred years ago.

(8) Opponents point out that the stations are expensive, costing about $1,200 each. (9) The stations are obviously worth it, and anyone who disagrees just doesn't care about the planet. (10) In fact, the parent association has offered to pay for half of the stations through its spring fundraiser.

(11) So yeah, refill stations would be pretty cool.$q$, 'draft')
