   $q$Sentence (2) does not help introduce the claim. Which revision of sentence (2) best leads into the claim in sentence (3)?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Some people like computers a lot more than other people do.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"keeps-irrelevant-idea"},{"text":"Many students enjoy playing video games after school.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-detail"},{"text":"Yet many students at our school never learn how computer programs actually work.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Computers were much larger and slower in the past.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Yet many students at our school never learn how computer programs actually work.$q$, $q$The correct revision names a gap that the claim in sentence (3) would fill, so it leads smoothly into the claim. The other choices are about likes, history, or games and do not set up a need for a coding course.$q$, 'draft', '9aab30c1-d84c-5302-9a2f-304cbee33f5f')
